---
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/Base.astro";
---

<PageLayout meta={{ title: "Research", description: "Research in development economics, labor markets, and public policy" }}>
  <section>
    <h1 class="title mb-8">Research</h1>

    <!-- Legend -->
    <div class="flex gap-5 flex-wrap mb-10 text-xs text-gray-500">
      <span class="flex items-center gap-2"><span style="width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;background:#1D9E75;display:inline-block;"></span> Working paper</span>
      <span class="flex items-center gap-2"><span style="width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;background:#B4B2A9;display:inline-block;"></span> Work in progress</span>
      <span class="flex items-center gap-2"><span style="width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;background:#7F77DD;display:inline-block;"></span> Publication</span>
      <span class="flex items-center gap-2"><span style="width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;background:#888780;display:inline-block;"></span> Other writing</span>
    </div>

    <!-- ── Working Papers ─────────────────────────────── -->
    <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-6">
      <span class="text-[10px] font-medium tracking-widest uppercase text-gray-500 whitespace-nowrap">Working Papers</span>
      <div class="flex-1 h-px bg-gray-700"></div>
      <span class="text-[10px] text-gray-600">3 papers</span>
    </div>

    <!-- Paper: Filling the Gaps -->
    <div class="py-5 border-b border-gray-800">
      <div class="flex gap-4">
        <div class="w-[3px] shrink-0 rounded-sm mt-1" style="background:#1D9E75;"></div>
        <div class="min-w-0">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-normal mb-1" style="font-family: 'Georgia', serif; line-height: 1.4;">
            Filling the Gaps? Private Sector Response to the Push and Pull of the Indian Public Schooling System
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mb-3">
            Prerna Dewan, Subhasish Dey, <strong class="text-gray-400 font-medium">Kasturi Kandalam</strong>, Abhiroop Mukhopadhyay, Soham Sahoo
          </p>
          <details class="group mb-3">
            <summary class="cursor-pointer text-xs text-gray-400 hover:text-gray-200 flex items-center gap-1.5 w-fit list-none">
              <span class="transform transition-transform duration-150 group-open:rotate-90 text-[8px]">▶</span>
              Abstract
            </summary>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-400 border-l border-gray-700 pl-4">
              We study how improvements in public school quality shape the evolution of local schooling markets in India.
              Combining district–year ASER test scores with the universe of UDISE administrative data for 2012–2017, we
              document a robust inverted-U relationship between public school quality and private school presence. When
              public schools perform poorly, marginal improvements in public test scores are associated with more private
              school entry — beyond a threshold, the relationship reverses. Private schools that remain in the market
              invest in more qualified teachers and better infrastructure, consistent with declining demand forcing quality
              upgrades.
            </p>
          </details>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3 flex-wrap">
            <div class="flex gap-1.5 flex-wrap flex-1">
              <span class="text-[10px] px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full bg-gray-800 text-gray-500 border border-gray-700">Private schools</span>
              <span class="text-[10px] px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full bg-gray-800 text-gray-500 border border-gray-700">Public schools</span>
              <span class="text-[10px] px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full bg-gray-800 text-gray-500 border border-gray-700">Education markets</span>
            </div>
            <a href="/kastkan/papers/The_Push_and_Pull_of_Public_Education_Quality.pdf"
               class="text-xs font-medium shrink-0"
               style="color:#1D9E75;"
               target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
              Draft PDF →
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Paper: Migration -->
    <div class="py-5 border-b border-gray-800">
      <div class="flex gap-4">
        <div class="w-[3px] shrink-0 rounded-sm mt-1" style="background:#1D9E75;"></div>
        <div class="min-w-0">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-normal mb-1" style="font-family: 'Georgia', serif; line-height: 1.4;">
            Where Have All the Men Gone? Temporary Migration &amp; Rural Public Works — A Discontinuity Approach
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mb-3">
            <strong class="text-gray-400 font-medium">Kasturi Kandalam</strong>
          </p>
          <details class="group mb-3">
            <summary class="cursor-pointer text-xs text-gray-400 hover:text-gray-200 flex items-center gap-1.5 w-fit list-none">
              <span class="transform transition-transform duration-150 group-open:rotate-90 text-[8px]">▶</span>
              Abstract
            </summary>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-400 border-l border-gray-700 pl-4">
              This paper examines the impact of NREGS on temporary migration in India using a fuzzy regression
              discontinuity design that exploits the phased rollout of the program. Drawing on NSS
              Employment–Unemployment Survey data (2007–08), the study finds that NREGS significantly increased
              seasonal migration of young males while the effect on young females was negligible. The results suggest
              NREGS enabled male migration either by substituting female labor into public works or by reducing
              migration risks through the availability of fallback employment.
            </p>
          </details>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3 flex-wrap">
            <div class="flex gap-1.5 flex-wrap flex-1">
              <span class="text-[10px] px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full bg-gray-800 text-gray-500 border border-gray-700">Migration</span>
              <span class="text-[10px] px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full bg-gray-800 text-gray-500 border border-gray-700">MGNREGA</span>
              <span class="text-[10px] px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full bg-gray-800 text-gray-500 border border-gray-700">Fuzzy RDD</span>
              <span class="text-[10px] px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full bg-gray-800 text-gray-500 border border-gray-700">India</span>
            </div>
            <a href="/kastkan/papers/migration_nregs_draft.pdf"
               class="text-xs font-medium shrink-0"
               style="color:#1D9E75;"
               target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
              Draft PDF →
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Paper: Charminar -->
    <div class="py-5 border-b border-gray-800">
      <div class="flex gap-4">
        <div class="w-[3px] shrink-0 rounded-sm mt-1" style="background:#1D9E75;"></div>
        <div class="min-w-0">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-normal mb-1" style="font-family: 'Georgia', serif; line-height: 1.4;">
            From Charminar to Cyberabad: Political Economy of Software Industry in Erstwhile Unified Andhra Pradesh
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mb-3">
            <strong class="text-gray-400 font-medium">Kasturi Kandalam</strong>
          </p>
          <details class="group mb-3">
            <summary class="cursor-pointer text-xs text-gray-400 hover:text-gray-200 flex items-center gap-1.5 w-fit list-none">
              <span class="transform transition-transform duration-150 group-open:rotate-90 text-[8px]">▶</span>
              Abstract
            </summary>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-400 border-l border-gray-700 pl-4">
              This paper draws on primary qualitative data and secondary quantitative data from erstwhile unified
              Andhra Pradesh to examine how ICT policies at the central and state levels led to a rise in the IT
              ecosystem. Drawing on 45 semi-structured interviews across stakeholders, I adopt a political economy
              framework to show how AP's policies changed the state's economic dynamic by mobilising labour and
              capital, and made the "techie" career aspirational.
            </p>
          </details>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3 flex-wrap">
            <div class="flex gap-1.5 flex-wrap flex-1">
              <span class="text-[10px] px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full bg-gray-800 text-gray-500 border border-gray-700">IT Industry</span>
              <span class="text-[10px] px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full bg-gray-800 text-gray-500 border border-gray-700">State Reforms</span>
              <span class="text-[10px] px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full bg-gray-800 text-gray-500 border border-gray-700">Andhra Pradesh</span>
            </div>
            <a href="/kastkan/papers/software_industry_ap_draft.pdf"
               class="text-xs font-medium shrink-0"
               style="color:#1D9E75;"
               target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
              Draft PDF →
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ── Work in Progress ───────────────────────────── -->
    <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-6 mt-12">
      <span class="text-[10px] font-medium tracking-widest uppercase text-gray-500 whitespace-nowrap">Work in Progress</span>
      <div class="flex-1 h-px bg-gray-700"></div>
      <span class="text-[10px] text-gray-600">2 projects</span>
    </div>

    <!-- WIP: Meghalaya -->
    <div class="py-5 border-b border-gray-800">
      <div class="flex gap-4">
        <div class="w-[3px] shrink-0 rounded-sm mt-1" style="background:#B4B2A9;"></div>
        <div class="min-w-0">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-normal mb-1" style="font-family: 'Georgia', serif; line-height: 1.4;">
            Gender, Geography, and Healthcare Utilization: Evidence from Insurance Claims in Meghalaya
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mb-2">
            <strong class="text-gray-400 font-medium">Kasturi Kandalam</strong>
          </p>
          <span class="text-[10px] font-medium tracking-wide uppercase px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full bg-gray-800 text-gray-500">Analysis in progress</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- WIP: Who Knows Best -->
    <div class="py-5 border-b border-gray-800">
      <div class="flex gap-4">
        <div class="w-[3px] shrink-0 rounded-sm mt-1" style="background:#B4B2A9;"></div>
        <div class="min-w-0">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-normal mb-1" style="font-family: 'Georgia', serif; line-height: 1.4;">
            Who Knows Best? (Dis)agreement on Reported Participation of Women in Intra-Household Decision-Making
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mb-2">
            <strong class="text-gray-400 font-medium">Kasturi Kandalam</strong> and Rosa Abraham
          </p>
          <span class="text-[10px] font-medium tracking-wide uppercase px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full bg-gray-800 text-gray-500">Analysis in progress</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ── Academic Writing ───────────────────────────── -->
    <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-6 mt-12">
      <span class="text-[10px] font-medium tracking-widest uppercase text-gray-500 whitespace-nowrap">Academic Writing</span>
      <div class="flex-1 h-px bg-gray-700"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="py-5 border-b border-gray-800">
      <div class="flex gap-4">
        <div class="w-[3px] shrink-0 rounded-sm mt-1" style="background:#7F77DD;"></div>
        <div class="min-w-0">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-normal mb-1" style="font-family: 'Georgia', serif; line-height: 1.4;">
            Shadow Banking in India: Nature, Trends, Concerns, and Policy Interventions
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mb-2">
            Kandalam, K., Sivramkrishna, S., Gune, S. &amp; Moharir, A. (2019).
            <em>Review of Economic and Business Studies (REBS)</em>, pp. 29–46.
          </p>
          <a href="http://rebs.feaa.uaic.ro/articles/pdfs/272.pdf"
             class="text-xs font-medium"
             style="color:#7F77DD;"
             target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            View publication →
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ── Other Writing ──────────────────────────────── -->
    <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-6 mt-12">
      <span class="text-[10px] font-medium tracking-widest uppercase text-gray-500 whitespace-nowrap">Other Writing</span>
      <div class="flex-1 h-px bg-gray-700"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="py-5 border-b border-gray-800">
      <div class="flex gap-4">
        <div class="w-[3px] shrink-0 rounded-sm mt-1" style="background:#888780;"></div>
        <div class="min-w-0">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-normal mb-1" style="font-family: 'Georgia', serif; line-height: 1.4;">
            There Are No Toilets in This Colony
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mb-2">
            Kandalam, K. &amp; Nakum, K. (2023). <em>People's Archive of Rural India (PARI)</em>.
          </p>
          <a href="https://ruralindiaonline.org/te/articles/there-are-no-toilets-in-this-colony/"
             class="text-xs font-medium text-gray-500 hover:text-gray-300"
             target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            Read article →
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="py-5">
      <div class="flex gap-4">
        <div class="w-[3px] shrink-0 rounded-sm mt-1" style="background:#888780;"></div>
        <div class="min-w-0">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-normal mb-1" style="font-family: 'Georgia', serif; line-height: 1.4;">
            Comparing Husband's and Wife's Perceptions of Women's Decision-Making Role
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mb-2">
            Kandalam, K. (2023). <em>State of Working India: Social Identities and Labour Market Outcomes</em>, p. 191.
            Centre for Sustainable Employment (CSE).
          </p>
          <a href="https://publications.azimpremjiuniversity.edu.in/5166/1/State_of_Working_India_2023_ebook_revised.pdf"
             class="text-xs font-medium text-gray-500 hover:text-gray-300"
             target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            Read article →
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </section>
</PageLayout>